-- title:
--   S-prime classes: Galois-stable part equals the closure
-- statement:
--   Let $E$ and $F$ be fields with $F$ a number field and $F$ an $E$-algebra, and let $S$ be a set of rational primes. Write $\mathcal{O}_F$ for the ring of integers of $F$; for a height-one prime $w$ of $\mathcal{O}_F$ let `primeClass F w` be the class in $\mathrm{Cl}(\mathcal{O}_F)$ of the ideal $w$, regarded via `ClassGroup.mk0` as a non-zero-divisor element of the ideal monoid, and let `placesOverPrimes F S` be the set of height-one primes $w$ such that the image of $p$ in $\mathcal{O}_F$ lies in $w$ for some $p \in S$. By definition `sPrimeClasses E F S` is the infimum, over all $E$-algebra automorphisms $\sigma$ of $F$, of the preimages of $\mathrm{Subgroup.closure}(\mathrm{primeClass}\,F\,[\mathrm{placesOverPrimes}\,F\,S])$ under the monoid homomorphism of $\mathrm{Cl}(\mathcal{O}_F)$ given by the action of $\sigma$. The theorem asserts that this infimum equals $\mathrm{Subgroup.closure}(\mathrm{primeClass}\,F\,[\mathrm{placesOverPrimes}\,F\,S])$ itself: cutting out the part stable under all $E$-automorphisms imposes no condition, because the subgroup generated by the classes of the primes above $S$ is already stable.
--
--   This identifies the Galois-stably defined subgroup of $S$-prime classes with the naive subgroup generated by the classes of the primes of $F$ above $S$, so that the two spellings of the $S$-class group quotient may be used interchangeably. It is used in the construction of the $S$-class group representation and in the comparison of that representation with $S$-unit cohomology and with $p$-torsion of $S$-classes.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_NumberField_LevelArith_sPrimeClasses_eq_closure.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_GroupCohomology_ContinuousUnramified
import Definitions.Def_DualSelmer_ExtConditions
import Definitions.Def_ExtCitation_KummerBridge
import Definitions.Def_GroupCohomology_ContinuousUnramifiedLevel
import Definitions.Def_GroupCohomology_ContinuousUnramifiedLevelMap
import Definitions.Def_NumberField_LevelArithmeticModP

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false
open NumberField.LevelArith
open scoped NumberField.LevelArith

theorem NumberField.LevelArith.sPrimeClasses_eq_closure
    (E F : Type) [Field E] [Field F] [NumberField F] [Algebra E F] (S : Set Nat.Primes) :
    sPrimeClasses E F S = Subgroup.closure (primeClass F '' placesOverPrimes F S) := by sorry
